This project uses a generic AI-First Architecture.

To maintain consistency across different AI tools (Cursor, Copilot, Gemini, Claude, etc.), ALL AI coding assistants must strictly follow the rules and workflows defined in the `.ai/` directory and `AGENTS.md`.

Before writing any code or answering questions, you MUST read and understand:
1. `.ai/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`   (Project domain, tech stack, architecture, business rules)
2. `.ai/LESSONS_LEARNED.md`   (Project memory, gotchas, pitfalls, user corrections)
3. `.ai/AI_WORKFLOW.md`       (Step-by-step workflow: Plan -> Code -> Verify -> Memory -> Commit)
4. `.ai/TASTESKILL.md`        (Design guidelines & Architecture rules)

Do NOT deviate from these guidelines.
Do NOT mix architectural patterns (Follow the tech stack defined in PROJECT_CONTEXT.md).
Do NOT commit without updating .ai/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md and .ai/LESSONS_LEARNED.md when adding features or finding gotchas.
Do NOT commit without following Conventional Commits format.
